  message: "NOT a duplicate of WI-vokiz (SimHash flagged it at 8 bits). WI-vokiz is tree_sitter Node.text being bytes|None at unguarded decode sites; this is the taint-catalogue merge replacing a shipped sink. No overlap beyond both being P-level defects in packages/*/src. Recording here because 'tracker update --not-duplicate-of' is what the warning text tells you to run and that flag does not exist on 'update' in this version."  # 80d9
- op: discuss  # cb32
  at: '2026-08-14T09:45:45Z'  # cb32
  by: agent  # cb32
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cb32
  clock: 3  # cb32
  nonce: cb32  # cb32
  message: "REPRO CONFIRMED ON THE CURRENT TREE, with an isolating fixture and the\nverdict-level trace inspected rather than inferred.\n\n  repo: one file — os.environ[\"API_KEY\"] -> os.remove(secret)\n  claim: {source_taint: host_secret, prohibited_sink_zone: host_fs}\n\n  baseline                                    rc 1  violated\n  + --taint-sinks re-declaring os.remove\n    into a `dev_zone` / trusted row           rc 0  confirmed\n\n  --json on the suppressed run:\n      verdicts[0].verdict = 'confirmed'\n      verdicts[0].caveats = []          <-- NO TRACE ON THE VERDICT\n\nSo the filed mechanism holds exactly. One correction to the record and one\nsharpening, both from running it:\n\nCORRECTION — THE FILED SPELLING OF THE OVERLAY DOES NOT LOAD. The item's\ndescription shows a sink row as a flat list under `sinks:`. The loader rejects\nthat outright (\"'sinks:' must be a dict, got list\", rc 2). The schema is\n`sinks: {<language>: [ {module, functions|methods} ]}` with `zone` and\n`trust_level` at the DOCUMENT level. That matters because it is the same\nINV-fokik slot-shape hazard the item already documents about `module` vs\n`name`: a wrong spelling here is LOUD (rc 2), while the wrong spelling the item\nwarns about is SILENT. Worth stating that the two failure modes differ.\n\nSHARPENING — THE COVERAGE GATE CAN MASK THE SUPPRESSION, AND WHETHER IT DOES IS\nINCIDENTAL. A first attempt used `Path(\"/tmp/out\").write_text(secret)`. The\ndisplacement still happened, but the verdict came back `inconclusive` rc 2 —\nnot because anything caught the displacement, but because `pathlib` was\nunclassified on that fixture (a chained-call receiver, INV-linub's shape) and\nthe blindness gate fires before confirmation. Swapping to `os.remove`, which\nclassifies cleanly, produced the `confirmed` rc 0 above.\n\nThe honest reading: a displaced sink ALWAYS suppresses the finding; whether the\nrun then reaches `confirmed` or is caught by an unrelated coverage gap is luck.\nOn a repo with complete coverage — which is the whole point of the coverage\nwork — it reaches `confirmed`. So closing coverage gaps makes this channel MORE\ndangerous, not less. That is an argument for fixing it before the coverage work\nlands, not after.\n\nWHAT DOES FIRE. INV-zosun's run-level provenance works and names the file:\n`catalog_provenance.taint_sinks.cli` carries the path and `user_supplied: true`.\nSo the run discloses \"a user catalogue was used\"; it does not disclose \"and it\nremoved the sink that would have caught this claim\". The verdict — the machine\nsurface a consumer branches on — is byte-identical to an honest confirm.\n\nFIX SHAPE, now costed. `_merge_with_user_override` already computes exactly the\ndisplacement set (the auto entries it filters out); it just throws it away.\nReturn it, carry it on TaintCatalog, and raise a third caveat kind alongside\nCAVEAT_USER_SUPPLIED_SANITIZER and CAVEAT_OPAQUE_BOUNDARY when a displaced\nSHIPPED sink's zone equals the claim's `prohibited_sink_zone` (or a displaced\nshipped source's label equals its `source_taint`) — i.e. precisely when the\nuser's row could have deleted THIS claim's evidence, rather than on every\ndisplacement, which would over-report. Verdict goes `confirmed` ->\n`confirmed_with_caveats` rc 3, the same downgrade INV-pojib established.\n\nThe zone/label filter is what keeps it a qualified opinion rather than noise: a\nuser row moving a sink INTO the prohibited zone adds findings and needs no\ncaveat.\n\nNOT SWEPT, unchanged from the filing: whether the same displacement can suppress\non the BOUNDARY arm via io_primitives overlays."  # cb32
